# =============================================================================
# Aerodrome — .gitignore
# =============================================================================
# Lines are grouped by category with a comment header explaining the rationale
# for each group. The runtime / local-only set matches the auto_created list in
# scripts/check_docs.py — keep them in sync if either changes.
# =============================================================================

# --- Python build/cache artifacts ---
# __pycache__/ and *.pyc are generated automatically by the Python runtime
# and have no reason to be in source control. *.egg-info/ won't typically
# appear since Aerodrome doesn't package as a wheel, but the line is cheap.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# --- Virtual environment ---
# install.sh creates ./venv/ on every install. It belongs to the host, not
# the repo. Both common naming conventions covered.
venv/
.venv/

# --- Runtime data ---
# The SQLite database (and its WAL/SHM sidecars) is the user's flight history
# and should never appear in the source tree. The wildcard catches any *.db
# file, not just the canonical aircraft_history.db, in case a developer
# creates a scratch DB during testing.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
.tracker.pid

# --- Logs ---
# install.sh creates the logs/ directory at runtime; tracker.log etc. live
# inside. Nothing in there should be committed.
logs/

# --- Live config ---
# config.yaml is the user's live, customized configuration. The shipped
# template is config.yaml.example; the live config is generated from it on
# first install and edited per-user. Auto-merge backups (config.yaml.bak.*)
# created by main.py during config-merge-on-startup also stay out.
config.yaml
config.yaml.bak.*

# --- Install backup snapshots ---
# The /api/updates/local/apply flow snapshots the live install to
# .backups/<timestamp>/ before swapping in a new release. These are
# host-specific recovery state, not source.
.backups/

# --- Update staging ---
# update/ is the staging area for the in-app updater. The folder itself is
# kept in the tree (via .gitkeep) so the install layout is correct on a
# fresh clone, and UPDATE_README.md inside is shipped documentation.
# Everything else in update/ is transient staging from an update in
# progress and stays out of source control.
update/*
!update/.gitkeep
!update/UPDATE_README.md

# --- tools/ is part of the product ---
# v3.4.12: previously tools/ was excluded here as "maintainer-only dev
# tooling" — the original v2.98.2 design shipped the synthetic feeder
# as a paired archive artifact alongside releases. That stopped being
# true in v3.1.0 when demo mode landed: bootstrap-menu installs that
# pick demo mode run tools/synthetic_feeder/serve.py as a real
# service, so the synthetic feeder has to be inside the release zip.
# scripts/package-release.sh was updated then to include tools/ in
# the zip, but this gitignore line was left behind, creating a
# discoverability gap — the public-repo and the release-zip surfaces
# disagreed about whether the synthetic feeder existed.
#
# v3.4.12 removes the exclusion so the public repo matches what
# users actually get from the release zip. tools/ is now tracked
# alongside the rest of the codebase.

# --- Editor / IDE clutter ---
# Personal preferences, not project state.
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# --- OS metadata ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# --- Release artifacts ---
# scripts/package-release.sh writes the release zip and .sha256 to the
# parent of the project tree, so they shouldn't normally land here. The
# patterns below are defensive — they keep accidental in-tree builds out
# of commits if the script is ever invoked from somewhere unexpected.
aerodrome-v*.zip
aerodrome-v*.zip.sha256

# Maintainer + agent-only — never public
.claude/
CLAUDE.md
HANDOFF.md
HANDOFF*.md
*-HANDOFF.md
AGENT_GUARDRAILS.md
